    "updated_at": "2023-12-21T09:04:03Z",
    "body": "I think there are some subtle incompatibilities indeed. E.g., a browser can produce `/%%` as a path. I haven't attempted to write exhaustive web-platform-tests for this though. That would probably be good. Testing how clients and servers deal with such \"incorrect\" (from the perspective of the HTTP specification anyway) paths would be good too. The result of such testing we can then use to determine where we need to make changes.",
